title: "breast-mri-core: late-phase removal and SER-filtered tumor volume in breast MRI (analysis code and derived scores)"
type: software
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-18"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Institute-of-One/breast-mri-core"
doi: "10.5281/zenodo.22822698"
identifiers:
  - type: doi
    value: "10.5281/zenodo.22822699"
    description: >-
      The archived version 0.1.0, as cited in the manuscript. The DOI above always resolves
      to the latest version.
abstract: >-
  Analysis code and derived scores for a study of how removing the late post-contrast
  phase changes signal-enhancement-ratio-filtered functional tumor volume in breast MRI,
  and how much that change affects discrimination of pathological complete response.
  Uses the public ACRIN-6698 / I-SPY 2 collection of The Cancer Imaging Archive (BMMR2
  training subset, 117 participants). Contains the paired patient scores, a script that
  reproduces all 20 reported AUC comparisons and bootstrap intervals to within 1e-12,
  an archival snapshot of the image-processing and analysis scripts, and a decomposition of
  each AUC difference into the patient pairs it reorders. No MRI data.
